00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:25.910
This video introduces functions and their
domains and ranges. A function is a correspondence

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:32.320
between input numbers, usually the x values
and output numbers, usually the y values,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:38.450
that sends each input number to exactly one
output number. Sometimes a function is thought

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:48.070
of as a rule or machine, in which you can
feed in x values as input and get out y values

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:54.600
as output. So, non mathematical example of
a function might be the biological mother

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:02.540
function, which takes as input and a person,
and it gives us output their biological mother.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:09.939
This function satisfies the condition that
each input number object person, in this case,

00:01:09.939 --> 00:01:16.670
get sent to exactly one output person. Because
if you take any person, they just have one

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:23.340
biological mother. So that rule does give
you a function. But if I change things around,

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:30.380
and just use the the mother function, which
sends to each person, their mother, that's

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.000
no longer gonna be a function, because there
are some people who have more than one mother,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:39.040
right, they could have a biological mother
and adopted mother, or a mother and stepmother

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:44.520
or any number of situations. So since there's,
there's at least some people who you would

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:50.340
put it as input, and then you'd get like more
than one possible output that violates this,

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:54.720
this rule of functions, that would not be
a function. Now, most of the time, we'll work

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.619
with functions that are described with equations,
not in terms of mothers. So for example, we

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:06.670
can have the function y equals x squared plus
one. This can also be written as f of x equals

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:12.810
x squared plus one. Here, f of x is function
notation that stands for the output value

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:20.349
of y. Notice that this notation is not representing
multiplication, we're not multiplying f by

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:26.900
x, instead, we're going to be putting in a
value for access input and getting out a value

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:34.260
of f of x or y. For example, if we want to
evaluate f of two, we're plugging in two as

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:42.840
input for x either in this equation, or in
that equation. Since F of two means two squared

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:51.219
plus one, f of two is going to equal five.
Similarly, f of five means I plug in five

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:58.739
for x. So that's going to be five squared
plus one, or 26. Sometimes it's useful to

00:02:58.739 --> 00:03:03.739
evaluate a function on a more complicated
expression involving other variables. In this

00:03:03.739 --> 00:03:08.500
case, remember, the functions value on any
expression, it's just what you what you get

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:17.330
when you plug in that whole expression for
x. So f of a plus three is going to be the

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:25.989
quantity a plus three squared plus one, we
could rewrite that as a squared plus six a

00:03:25.989 --> 00:03:33.650
plus nine plus one, or a squared plus six
a plus 10. When evaluating a function on a

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:39.890
complex expression, it's important to keep
the parentheses when you plug in for x. That

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:47.799
way, you evaluate the function on the whole
expression. For example, it would be wrong

00:03:47.799 --> 00:03:55.180
to write f of a plus three equals a plus three
squared plus one without the parentheses,

00:03:55.180 --> 00:04:00.880
because that would imply we were just squaring
the three and not the whole expression, a

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:09.069
plus three. Sometimes the function is described
with a graph instead of an equation. In this

00:04:09.069 --> 00:04:16.920
example, this graph is supposed to represent
the function g of x. Not all graphs actually

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:22.900
represent functions. For example, the graph
of a circle doesn't represent a function.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:27.830
That's because the graph of a circle violates
the vertical line test, you can draw a vertical

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:33.730
line, and I'll intersect the graph in more
than one point. But our graph it left satisfies

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:38.590
the vertical line test, any vertical line
intersects the graph, and at most one point,

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:44.020
that means is a function because every x value
will have at most one y value that corresponds

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:52.639
to it. Let's evaluate gf two, note that two
